==Grammar==
The system of [[personal pronoun]]s in Lemerig contrasts [[clusivity]], and distinguishes four [[Grammatical number|numbers]] (singular, [[Dual number|dual]], [[Trial number|trial]], and plural).{{sfn|François|2016}}

Most negative morphemes are discontinuous, wrapped around the predicate phrase: e.g. {{IPA|/(ɛʔ) … (k​͡pʷæl) ʔæ/}} (Negative realis ‘did~does not’), {{IPA|/(ɛʔ) … ʔæ kiʔi(s)/}} (Nondumitive ‘not yet’), {{IPA|/mɛ … ŋ​͡mʷæs-ʔæ/}} (Negative potential ‘cannot’).{{sfn|François|2026|p=127}} Historically, this pattern reflects an instance of [[Jespersen's cycle]].{{sfn|François|2026|p=115}}

Spatial reference in Lemerig is based on a system of geocentric ([[Linguistic frame of reference#Absolute frame of reference|absolute]]) directionals, which is in part typical of [[Oceanic languages]], in part innovative.{{sfn|François|2015|pp=169–170}}

